# plans/plan_dx9.md D9-A5 scene corpus: colored_linestrip_quad
# The third and final never-before-exercised PrimitiveType in the corpus, completing all 4 real
# XNA PrimitiveType values (TriangleList was already covered by every other scene;
# TriangleStrip/LineList were closed by colored_trianglestrip_quad/colored_linelist_quad).
# PrimitiveType.LineStrip draws N-1 CONNECTED line segments from N vertices -- a single continuous
# polyline, genuinely different from LineList's independent segments even given similar-looking
# vertex data. No code changes needed: GraphicsDevice::PrimitiveVerts()/ToD3D9Topology() already
# handle LineStrip unconditionally.
#
# Three vertices forming an open "V" / zigzag polyline (not a closed shape): top-left -> bottom ->
# top-right. This is the key discriminator from LineList: the scene harness computes
# primitiveCount from vertex count per-PrimitiveType (GraphicsDevice::PrimitiveVerts()'s own
# inverse), so these 3 vertices become primitiveCount=2 under LineStrip (n-1) but would be
# malformed/rejected under LineList (n must be even, 3 isn't). Both segments genuinely render
# (confirmed on real XNA: 307 non-background pixels spanning the full x=[26,230]/y=[52,205]
# extent of the "V", with sample points at BOTH the left segment's own midpoint (~x=77,y=128) and
# the right segment's own midpoint (~x=179,y=128) reading pure RED) -- proving both connected
# segments draw from the shared middle vertex, not just one.
width=256
height=256
profile=HiDef
clearcolor=100,149,237,255
vertexcolor=true
lighting=false
primitive=LineStrip
vertex=-0.8,0.6,0,255,0,0,255
vertex=0.0,-0.6,0,255,0,0,255
vertex=0.8,0.6,0,255,0,0,255
